📜 Privacy Policy for Call App

Last updated: January 2026

Call App respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard data when you use our application.

1️⃣ Information We Collect
- Device information (for performance and compatibility)
- User account details (if login is enabled)
- Call and messaging metadata (not call content)
- Local network data (to enable local communication)

❌ We do NOT record calls, read messages, or access personal files.

2️⃣ How We Use Information
- Enable local calling and messaging
- Improve app performance and stability
- Fix bugs and enhance user experience
- Ensure security and prevent misuse

3️⃣ Data Sharing
- ❌ We do not sell or share your data with third parties
- ❌ No ads, trackers, or hidden analytics
- ✅ Data stays on your device or local network only

4️⃣ Permissions Used
- Microphone (for calls)
- Camera (for video calls, if enabled)
- Storage (optional, for media sharing)
- Network access (for communication)

All permissions are used strictly for app functionality.

5️⃣ Data Security
We use industry-standard security practices to protect your data. Local communication is prioritized to reduce external exposure.

6️⃣ Children’s Privacy
Call App is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from minors.

7️⃣ Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy when needed. Changes will be reflected within the app or on the app listing.

